10:T1712,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Recipe","mainEntityOfPage":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/","name":"Blackberry Fool","image":["https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/blackberry-fool.jpg","https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/blackberry-fool.jpg"],"datePublished":"2026-11-01","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"@crave_testkitchen"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Crave Recipes","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/icon-512.png","width":512,"height":512}},"description":"British-inspired blackberry fool with 13 measured ingredients — zero sign-up, instant Cook Mode. Ready in 45 mins (4 servings). 4.7★ rated with US/Metric scaling & hands-free Cook Mode.","prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT30M","totalTime":"PT45M","recipeYield":"4 servings","recipeCategory":"Global Classics","recipeCuisine":"British","keywords":"Blackberry Fool, British, Global Classics, #BlackberryFoo, #CraveMadeMeDoIt, #ViralDesserts, #BritishSweets","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"328 calories"},"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":4.7,"reviewCount":192},"recipeIngredient":["3.3 tbsp Hazlenuts","8.3 tbsp Butter","10 tbsp Caster Sugar","1 grated Lemon","10 tbsp Plain Flour","1 tsp Baking Powder","2.67 cup Blackberries","5 tbsp Sugar","2 tbs Caster Sugar","1 tbs Lemon Juice","1.25 cup Double Cream","6.7 tbsp Yogurt","1 garnish with Mint"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Prep & Mix: Blackberry Fool","text":"For the biscuits, preheat the oven to 200C/180C (fan)/Gas 6 and line two large baking trays with baking parchment. Scatter the nuts over a baking tray and roast in the oven for 6-8 minutes, or until golden-brown. Watch them carefully so that they don’t have a chance to burn. Remove from the oven, tip onto a board and leave to cool. Put the butter and sugar in a large bowl and beat with a wooden spoon until light and creamy. Roughly chop the cooled nuts and add to the creamed butter and sugar, along with the lemon zest, flour and baking powder. Stir well until the mixture comes together and forms a ball – you may need to use your hands. Divide the biscuit dough into 24 even pieces and roll into small balls. Place the balls the prepared baking trays, spaced well apart to allow for spreading. Incorporate 3.3 tbsp hazlenuts, 8.3 tbsp butter, 10 tbsp caster sugar, and 1 grated lemon smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Bake Until Golden & Set","text":"Press the biscuits to flatten to around 1cm/½in thick. Bake the biscuits, one tray at a time, for 12 minutes or until very pale golden-brown. Leave to cool on the trays. They will be very soft when you take them out of the oven, but will crisp as they cool. Store in an airtight tin and eat within five days. For the fool, rinse the blackberries in a colander to wash away any dust or dirt. Put the blackberries in a non-stick saucepan and sprinkle over the caster sugar. Incorporate 10 tbsp plain flour, 1 tsp baking powder, 2.67 cup blackberries, 5 tbsp sugar, 2 tbs caster sugar, 1 tbs lemon juice, 1.25 cup double cream, 6.7 tbsp yogurt, and 1 garnish with mint smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy","text":"Stir in the lemon juice and heat gently for two minutes, or until the blackberries begin to soften and release their juices. Remove and reserve 12 blackberries for decoration and continue cooking the rest. Simmer the blackberries very gently for 15 minutes, stirring regularly until very soft and squidgy. Remove from the heat and press the berries and juice through a sieve over a bowl, using the bottom of a ladle to help you extract as much of the purée as possible. Leave the purée to cool and discard the seeds. You should end up with around 325ml/11fl oz of purée. Put the cream and yoghurt in a large bowl and whip with an electric whisk until soft peaks form when the whisk is removed from the bowl – the acidity of the fruit will thicken the cream further, so don’t take it too far.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy","text":"When the purée is completely cold, adjust the sweetness to taste by adding more sugar if needed. Pour it into the bowl with the whipped cream and yoghurt and stir just once or twice until very lightly combined. Spoon the blackberry fool into individual wide, glass dishes – or one large, single bowl. It should look quite marbled, so don’t over-stir it. Scatter a few tiny mint leaves on top and decorate with the reserved blackberries. Sprinkle with a little sugar if you like and serve with the hazelnut biscuits.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/#step-4"}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Global Classics","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/category/global-viral/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Blackberry Fool","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/blackberry-fool/"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to make Blackberry Fool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Blackberry Fool takes 45 minutes total (15 minutes prep) and yields 4 servings at 328 calories per serving."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I make Blackberry Fool healthier or with zero refined sugar?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes! Toggle the Healthy Swap mode on this Blackberry Fool recipe page to convert ingredients into lower-sugar, higher-protein, or wholesome alternatives automatically."}}]}]}5:[["$","script",null,{"id":"crave-recipe-jsonld","type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$10"}}],"$L11","$L12"]
